  <title>Tables</title>
  <p>
    In some tables, such as a message list, speaking the full row can provide useful context. In
    other tables, such as a spreadsheet, speaking only the focused cell can make navigation
    faster and less verbose. The settings below control row presentation for different kinds of
    tables.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-tables">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Speech</gui> category, <gui>Tables</gui> group.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Row Navigation</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca speaks an entire row or only the focused cell when moving by row.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Speak full row in GUI tables</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca speaks the entire row or only the focused cell in application tables, such as
              a message list. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Speak full row in document tables</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca speaks the entire row or only the focused cell in document tables, such as
              Writer and web tables. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Speak full row in spreadsheets</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca speaks the entire row or only the focused cell in spreadsheets. Default: off.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Cell Navigation</gui>: Controls which cell
          details Orca speaks while navigating tables.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Speak cell header</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca speaks the header of a table cell. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Speak cell coordinates</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca speaks table cell coordinates in document content. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Speak spreadsheet cell coordinates</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca speaks spreadsheet cell coordinates. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Speak multiple cell spans</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca speaks how many rows and columns a cell spans. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Always speak selected spreadsheet range</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca speaks the full selected range when spreadsheet selection changes. Default:
              off.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
  <section id="commands-table-speech">
    <title>Commands</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Commands</gui> category, <gui>Commands</gui> section, <gui>Speech and verbosity</gui> group.
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Toggle whether to read just the current table cell or the whole row</gui>: <keyseq>
            <key>Orca Modifier</key>
            <key>F11</key>
          </keyseq>
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
